# Translations: ship the .pot and NOTHING else.
#
# Every locale comes from the wordpress.org language packs built off
# translate.wordpress.org, so a bundled catalogue is at best a duplicate and at
# worst an unreviewed translation in a package the polyglots team never saw.
# These rules are deliberately by FILE TYPE, not by locale. The previous list
# named locales one by one and `polski-bel.mo` walked straight through it,
# because the rule said `polski-be_BY.*`. A per-locale list rots every time a
# new catalogue appears; a per-extension list cannot.
#
# scripts/assert-package-clean.sh fails the build if anything but a .pot ends
# up in languages/, so this cannot silently regress again.
messages.mo
languages/*.po
languages/*.mo
languages/*.json
languages/*.l10n.php
languages/*.po~
languages/translate_po.py
languages/polski-pro.pot

# editor backups (never ship / never a badly_named_files reject)
*~
*.bak

# Translation import tooling (GlotPress PO/MO staging) - never ship in the zip
glotpress-import/
